{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ברעה", :translit "be-re'eh", :gloss "in seeing / shepherd"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Extra heh in be-re'eh hints to five (H = 5) sins committed at the golden calf."}], :frame {:text "The verse says Joshua heard the sound of the people ברעה (be-re'eh). The spelling with a final heh instead of the expected form is read as an allusion to five categories of transgression at the golden calf. Verse Exodus 32:6 records eating, drinking, and rising to make sport; verse Exodus 32:8 records bowing and sacrificing. The fifth element, dances, is supplied by Exodus Rabbah 41:7 and Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:1(10), which enumerate the five things Israel deserved punishment for at that event.", :sources ["Exodus 32:6" "Exodus 32:8" "Exodus Rabbah 41:7" "Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Extra heh in be-re'eh hints to five (H = 5) sins committed at the golden calf.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:20:34.237943135Z", :model "glm-5.2"}